**CRITICAL NOTE on "K"**

**K has DUAL STATES:**

\# Unpurified K (default):

\# - Kosha: Pranamaya

\# - Vritti: Vikalpa (Āśā - hope masking fear)

\# - Quality: Grasping, scanning, underlying fear

\# Purified K (after vowel + aspect lifting):

\# - Kosha: Vijnanamaya

\# - Vritti: Pramāṇa (discrimination)

\# - Quality: Sharp discernment

\# Example:

\# \"Ke\" (in \"Rakesh\") = K (unpurified) + E (forward desire)

\# → Base Kosha: Pranamaya (not Vijnanamaya!)

